# tmux validation (Agent shell commands)

When testing or validating tmux config, **never disrupt the user's default tmux server**.

## Forbidden on the default socket

- `tmux kill-server` (no `-L`)
- `tmux kill-session` on sessions the user is using (e.g. `nvim-dev`)
- Any command that stops or replaces the user's attached session

## Safe reload (live config)

Apply changes to a running server without restarting:

```bash
tmux source-file ~/.tmux.conf \; display-message "reloaded"
```

Read-only checks are safe: `tmux list-sessions`, `tmux list-keys`, etc.

## Isolated validation (preferred for tests)

Use a **separate socket** so cleanup cannot affect the user:

```bash
SOCK="agent-tmux-test-$$"
tmux -L "$SOCK" -f /path/to/.tmux.conf new-session -d -s test
# ... run checks ...
tmux -L "$SOCK" kill-server   # only kills the test server
```

Always pass `-L "$SOCK"` to every tmux command in that test block (including `kill-server`).

## Examples

```bash
# BAD — kills all user sessions
tmux kill-server

# GOOD — test server only
SOCK="agent-tmux-test-$$"
tmux -L "$SOCK" -f ~/.tmux.conf new-session -d && tmux -L "$SOCK" list-keys
tmux -L "$SOCK" kill-server
```
